    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000000": {
      "name": "What this map is about",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**What the flood of 26 August 2026 did, and what is still not known.**\n\nIt started with a mountain. At **08:40** that morning about a square kilometre\nbroke off a slope near the China border. For a few hours it was reported as an\nearthquake. It was not. It was the mountain hitting the valley floor.\n\nIt picked up water and mud on the way down, and ran **210 km** down four rivers\nin one day.\n\n**What is below**\n\n- Where it started, and what the satellites could not see\n- Three stretches of river, before and after, and why the damage fell where it did\n- Who died, and where: the damage is in the mountains, the dead are on the plain\n- Two new lakes that are still up there\n- Why no count of this flood is final\n\n*Scroll to begin.*\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What this map is about"
        },
        "extent": [
          9498532.138560558,
          3269579.387709147,
          9541642.622513851,
          3301338.972961972
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true
          },
          {
            "opacity": 1.0,
