    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000001": {
      "name": "The ground it came off",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**196 hectares of mountainside are gone.**\n\nThe scar was mapped from Landsat 9 images taken on the day it happened. NDRRMA\nput the mass that broke off at about a square kilometre of rock and old glacier\ndebris.\n\nIt sits above the Lhende Khola. That is a small river that joins the Bhote Koshi\nten kilometres below. Nothing up here could be damaged. Everything else in this\nmap happened downhill of it.\n\n**On the map:** the brown outline is where it broke away\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "40%",
          "title": "The ground it came off"
        },
        "extent": [
          9516003.425867312,
          3282450.5222409843,
          9524171.335207097,
          3288467.8384301346
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
