    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000004": {
      "name": "The steep gorge",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Here the riverbed drops 42.5 m every kilometre, and the valley walls are close\ntogether.**\n\nThe river used to be a thin line through forest. It is now bare rock from one\nwall to the other. In this 6 by 6 km box, **715 features** are marked destroyed.\nThat counts buildings, roads and bridges together. Three health posts were lost\ntoo: at Timure, Rasuwagadhi and Syafrubesi.\n\nOn ground this steep, the water hits instead of rising.\n\n**On the map:** bridges, dark red where lost\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "40%",
          "title": "The steep gorge"
        },
        "extent": [
          9490009.329558322,
          3271854.1076403414,
          9516546.945296166,
          3291404.4256174252
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
