    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000006": {
      "name": "The middle valley",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Six kilometres on, the bed is flatter, at 24.3 m per km. The valley is opening\nout.**\n\nA box of the same size holds **342** destroyed. That is less than half the gorge.\nThe ground is gentler here, so more people build on it. Downstream in Nuwakot\nalone, **1,267 houses** were fully damaged and\n**1,253** partly damaged.\n\n**On the map:** the blue fill is the water line that was observed\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "40%",
          "title": "The middle valley"
        },
