    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000010": {
      "name": "Why the three are different",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "fig-gradient-vs-damage.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**One thing explains all three: how steeply the riverbed falls.**\n\n![Bed gradient and bridge losses over the same three reaches](attachment:fig-gradient-vs-damage.png)\n\nA steep bed makes fast water. Fast water hits the bank with everything it is\ncarrying. Where the bed is flat, the river spreads out instead of cutting in.\n\n**16 of 16** bridges were lost in the\ngorge. **6 of 108** on the plain. In its report of\n1 September, NDRRMA counted **41 road bridges washed\naway** and 4 damaged along the whole river.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "58%",
          "title": "Why the three are different"
        },
        "extent": [
          9372057.742142433,
          3194194.0660533994,
          9522177.166500462,
          3304787.365380991
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
