    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000011": {
      "name": "Where it got to, and when",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The wave took most of a working day to cross the country. People timed it the\nwhole way.**\n\nGalchhi **10:28** \u00b7 Malekhu **11:50** \u00b7 Mugling **13:00** \u00b7 Devghat **15:20**. At Devghat it peaked about an hour later, at some **5,850 m\u00b3/s**.\n\nThose four places are 90, 115, 155 and 189 km down the river from the\nslope.\n\n**57.4 million m\u00b3** of water passed in all. About\n20.0 million of that was on top of what the\nriver was already carrying.\n\n**On the map:** four violet dots down the yellow reach, upstream to downstream\nin the order above, getting darker as the day goes on\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "40%",
          "title": "Where it got to, and when"
        },
        "extent": [
          9284715.981957538,
          3130021.744579748,
          9546089.080830684,
          3322575.8626325713
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true
          },
          {
