    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000012": {
      "name": "Destroyed upstream, killed downstream",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Nearly everything you have just seen destroyed was in the mountains. But most\nof the people who died were on the plain.**\n\nDeaths by district, as the Nepal Police counted them on 5 September:\n\n- **Chitwan 360**\n- **Nawalparasi West 230**, **East 222**\n- Nuwakot 192 \u00b7 Rasuwa 160 \u00b7 Gorkha 73 \u00b7 Dhading 67 \u00b7 Tanahun 38\n\n812 of 1,342 deaths are in the three districts\nfurthest from the mountain. That is where the flood was slowest and broke the\nleast. Rasuwa, where it tore the valley open, lost 160.\nFour days earlier that figure was 27.\n\nAlmost nobody lives in the gorge. The plain is where the people are. The flood\ndid the most damage where the ground was steepest. It killed where the people\nwere.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Destroyed upstream, killed downstream"
        },
        "extent": [
          9245186.985396827,
          3099260.4625948602,
          9590070.85702317,
          3353337.144617459
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
