    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000013": {
      "name": "The people",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**As of 7 September, the Kathmandu Post reported NDRRMA's count as:**\n\n- **1,355 dead**\n- **4,996 missing** \u2014 2,340 from Nuwakot, 1,967 from Rasuwa, 589 foreign nationals\n- **13,396 rescued**, and **6,672** treated for injuries\n\nFor six days after the water, **3,702 households,\n14,461 people** in Gosaikunda and Amachhodingmo were\ncompletely cut off. No road, no electricity, no telephone.\n\n**8 schools** were destroyed and 8 damaged,\nout of 19 checked. Together they taught\n6,901 pupils.\n\nThose last two figures are from 1 September. The district list on the card before\ncame to 1,342, counted by the Nepal Police two days earlier. Different bodies\ncount on different days, and [NDRRMA](https://bipadportal.gov.np/) publishes the\ncurrent ones.\n\n**On the map:** schools inside the flood extent, red where destroyed\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The people"
        },
        "extent": [
          9348387.468300542,
          3152557.86960285,
          9575925.966755012,
          3320185.965538724
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.25,
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
