    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000015": {
      "name": "What is still up there",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The debris blocked the river in places. Those blockages are still forming, and\nstill breaking.**\n\nUNOSAT saw two barrier lakes on images from 28 August,\n**20 ha** and\n**12 ha**. NDRRMA report that some have since\ndrained, and that more can form while the banks are loose and the rain keeps\ncoming.\n\nA pile of debris across a river is not a dam anyone built. Of 73 landslide dams\nwhose lifetime was known, Costa and Schuster found\n**27 per cent broke within a day**, and about half within ten days. Those shares\nonly describe dams that broke. Many never do.\n\nPawan Bhattarai of Tribhuvan University, quoted by Al Jazeera on 28 August: \"The\ndanger is not just the lake itself, but the possibility of sudden dam failure.\"\n\nThe valley below has lost its road and most of its bridges.\n\n**On the map:** the teal shapes are the two lakes \u00b7 brown is where the mountain\nbroke away\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "45%",
          "title": "What is still up there"
        },
        "extent": [
          9511069.747720994,
          3283806.8304174375,
          9523449.983221062,
          3292927.3762512645
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
